WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.441 --> 00:00:02.493
- [Voiceover] So you've moved to a city

00:00:02.493 --> 00:00:03.916
and bought a car.

00:00:03.916 --> 00:00:06.313
Now it's time to learn to drive

00:00:06.313 --> 00:00:07.604
like an (bleep) hole.

00:00:07.604 --> 00:00:10.294
("Jolly Shoppers")

00:00:10.294 --> 00:00:12.673
Last time on driving like an (bleep) hole

00:00:12.673 --> 00:00:15.192
we covered texting at red lights,

00:00:15.192 --> 00:00:17.975
tailgating, and driving 50 miles an hour

00:00:17.975 --> 00:00:19.235
in the left lane.

00:00:19.235 --> 00:00:21.449
This time, parking.

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:23.461
You're in a city so it's very important

00:00:23.461 --> 00:00:26.183
to learn how to park like an (bleep) hole.

00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:27.666
When looking for a spot,

00:00:27.666 --> 00:00:29.251
drive as slow as you want

00:00:29.251 --> 00:00:32.920
no matter how congested
the area is. (cars honking)

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.173
Oh look, an empty spot.

00:00:36.423 --> 00:00:37.824
Yes!

00:00:37.824 --> 00:00:40.324
There might be room for two cars here,

00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:42.193
but not the way you drive.

00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:44.367
Make sure you leave
plenty of room in between

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.175
you and the next bumper.

00:00:46.175 --> 00:00:48.532
Not enough room for a car, (buzzer sounds)

00:00:48.532 --> 00:00:51.132
just enough room for let's say a golf cart

00:00:51.132 --> 00:00:52.938
or a dolphin.

00:00:52.938 --> 00:00:54.362
Perfect.

00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:56.537
That'll make someone mad later.

00:00:56.537 --> 00:00:58.447
If you have a smaller car,

00:00:58.447 --> 00:01:01.879
parking garages are
just the place for you.

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:03.892
When in a crowded parking garage,

00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:07.407
make sure you go right
to the front of the spot.

00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:08.951
There it is.

00:01:08.951 --> 00:01:10.312
Make sure it's enough for someone

00:01:10.312 --> 00:01:13.155
to think they've finally
found an open one,

00:01:13.155 --> 00:01:15.295
only to crush their dreams.

00:01:17.565 --> 00:01:19.942
Don't worry about validating your ticket.

00:01:19.942 --> 00:01:23.437
You can probably just use
a credit card at the exit.

00:01:23.437 --> 00:01:25.103
(horns honking irritably)

00:01:25.103 --> 00:01:28.251
Next time we'll cover
never using your blinker,

00:01:28.251 --> 00:01:30.873
putting your entire
family's lives at risk,

00:01:30.873 --> 00:01:32.661
and making sure you get the most

00:01:32.661 --> 00:01:34.530
out of your insurance premium.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:39.530
(upbeat hip-hop music)

